commit 4fe871351053020cd4dde5970d3bc2abe7425e80
Author: kaigani <kaigani@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 13:31:47 2026 -0800

    fix(c2.3 r3): one acceptance boundary for every invocation; selection scans charge work
    
    A request whose caller timed out is refused before any of its changes is kept:
    the cancellation check now runs at the start of a single acceptance boundary
    shared by single invocations and atomic batches, before the frozen guard,
    pending saves, the document commit and effects, including the path with no
    document transaction. A refusal restores the saved session state in full.
    
    - Rollback also restores the agent hub's sessions and policy (confirmation
      requests and activity entries are kept, as before).
    - Settings changes (project.create last-used values and recent list,
      project.recent.remove) are deferred effects instead of handler writes.
    - Selection, bounds and point-selection scans charge a work account.
    - A cancelled work account's error no longer carries the geometry hint; the
      watchdog hint no longer says the call may still complete.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

